## Individual Configuration

The chart deploys all configured APIs, using the same default-configuration for each of them to make the deployment easier. However, it also allows to overwrite 
every configuration for the individual API as following:

While the default-config might set:
```yaml
  defaultConfig:
    replicaCount: 1
    image:
      # -- repository to get the container from
      repository: quay.io/wi_stefan
      # -- tag to be used, most of the time the apis will use the same version
      tag: 0.4.1
      # -- pull policy to be used
      pullPolicy: IfNotPresent
    # -- log level of the api
    logLevel: WARN
    # -- cache config for connecting the broker
    cache:
      # -- maximum size of the cache
      maximumSize: 1000
      # -- how fast should the cache entry expire after it was written?
      expireAfterWrite: 2s
```

Those values can be overwritten on an individual API level as following:

```yaml
apis:
  # uses the default
  - name: party-catalog
    image: tmforum-party-catalog
    basePath: /tmf-api/party/v4

  # customized
  - name: product-catalog
    image: tmforum-product-catalog
    basePath: /tmf-api/productCatalogManagement/v4
    replicaCount: 3
    image:
      repository: quay.io/my_own_repo
      tag: 1.2.3
      pullPolicy: Always
    logLevel: DEBUG
    cache:
      maximumSize: 3000
```
For all untouched values, the customized deployement will still use the defaults, while the explicitly set once are overwritten.

## UI

[tmf-ui](https://github.com/FIWARE/tmforum-api/tree/main/ui) is a read-only web browser for the APIs: it lists the
entities and follows the references between them as hyperlinks. It only ever issues `GET`. Enable it with
`ui.enabled: true`:

- With `allInOne.enabled: true` it runs as a **sidecar** of the all-in-one and reads from it on `localhost`.
- Otherwise it runs as a **deployment of its own** and reads through the `apiProxy`, which has to be enabled: the
  UI needs every API under a single origin. (`ui.endpoint` points it anywhere else.)

Either way it is reachable through the `<fullname>-ui` service:

```shell
kubectl port-forward svc/<fullname>-ui 8080:8080
# http://localhost:8080/
```

It has no authentication of its own: whoever reaches the service reads the APIs. Do not expose it publicly.
The `tmforum-ui` image is only published by tmforum-api releases newer than 1.18.6; until `appVersion` points at one,
set `ui.image.tag`.

In split mode the UI only finds the APIs at the base paths of the all-in-one: the default `party-role` base path
(`/tmf-api/partyRoleManagement/v4`) differs from it (`/tmf-api/partyRole/v4`), and `document-management` is not
deployed, so both show up as unreachable.

